RudeCGI NEWS - User visible changes.
See ChangeLog for more detailed information on internal changes
See the end for copying conditions.


__________________________________________________________________________________
Release 5.2.0 - Matthew Flood 2026-07-30

	- BEHAVIOR CHANGE: cookies are now parsed after form data on POST
	  requests, as they already were on GET.  Cookies and form fields
	  share one lookup namespace, and the old order let a client-supplied
	  cookie shadow a POST field at every unindexed value() call.  Both
	  values are still present and reachable by index, and datasource()
	  still reports the origin of each; only the unindexed lookup changes,
	  and only on POST.
	- BEHAVIOR CHANGE: value(index) and value(fieldname, position) now
	  return NULL when the index or position is out of bounds, as cgi.h
	  has always documented.  They returned the empty string instead, so
	  the enumeration loop printed in the header's own example -
	
	      while(category = parser->value("cat", x++))
	
	  - never terminated.  value(fieldname) is unchanged: it still
	  returns "" for an unknown field and never returns NULL.
	- contenttype() now returns "application/x-formdata" for data that is
	  not an uploaded file, which is the default cgi.h documents.  It
	  returned the empty string, so that documented value appeared
	  nowhere in the library.
	- New CGI::maxPostReadSeconds(long) bounds how long reading the POST
	  body will wait.  A client that over-declares CONTENT_LENGTH and then
	  holds the connection open used to pin the process indefinitely,
	  because fread() blocks until it has the full count or reaches EOF.
	  The default is unchanged (wait indefinitely); whatever arrives
	  within the limit is parsed.  POSIX only - on Windows the limit is
	  ignored, since select() there does not apply to pipes.

__________________________________________________________________________________
Release 5.1.1 - Matthew Flood 2026-07-30

	- SECURITY: fixed disclosure of uninitialised heap memory through
	  POSTed field values.  The POST buffer was allocated but never
	  zeroed and fread()'s return value was ignored, so a CONTENT_LENGTH
	  larger than the body actually sent left the tail of the buffer
	  uninitialised - and it was parsed and returned to the caller as
	  field data.  Only the bytes actually read are now parsed.
	- Fixed crash on a missing CONTENT_LENGTH.  The value was passed
	  straight to atoi(), which dereferences NULL when the variable is
	  absent - as it is for any GET, any POST with no body, and any run
	  from a shell.  CGI::maxPostLength() did not prevent this because
	  the cap was applied after the atoi() call; it is now applied
	  before anything is parsed or allocated.
	- CONTENT_LENGTH is now validated: negative values, non-numeric
	  values, trailing garbage and values beyond INT_MAX are rejected
	  rather than silently reinterpreted, and an outsized declared
	  length can no longer abort the process through std::bad_alloc.
	- Fixed pkg-config file: it hardcoded the prefix given at configure
	  time, so installing with "cmake --install --prefix <dir>" produced
	  a rudecgi.pc still pointing at the configure-time prefix (by
	  default /usr/local).  The prefix is now relative to ${pcfiledir}.
	- Removed the last references to the CGI::instance() method from the
	  installed header.  5.1.0 corrected this in the README but left the
	  doc comments in cgi.h teaching an API that does not exist.
	- CGI::version() now reports the release version.  It returned a
	  hardcoded "RudeServer CGI Version 3.0" that had not tracked a
	  release since before 4.0, so callers could not tell what they had
	  linked.  The value is now generated from the build so it cannot
	  drift again.
	- Added regression tests for all of the above, including scenarios
	  that crash or leak under AddressSanitizer without these fixes.

__________________________________________________________________________________
Release 5.1.0 - Matthew Flood 2026-07-30

	- New CMake build system (autotools files retained but deprecated);
	  installs CMake package config and pkg-config files.
	- Code modernized to compile cleanly as C++17 with -Wall -Wextra
	  (const-correct hex table in the URL decoder, ctype calls made
	  safe for high-bit/UTF-8 input on signed-char platforms, fixed a
	  mismatched delete on uploaded-file names).
	- Added test suite (ctest) covering GET query strings, POST bodies,
	  and cookies, plus GitHub Actions CI on Linux x86_64/ARM, macOS,
	  and Windows, and an ASan/UBSan job.
	- New README with verified quick-start example and a correction:
	  the documented CGI::instance() method never existed in this API;
	  simply construct a rude::CGI object.

